Below is a collection of tweets posted by {{ name }} on Twitter/X. Every line is a single tweet already attributed to {{ name }} — no speaker identification needed.

Note on the source: tweets are short, unfiltered, and highly distilled. They lack conversational filler and show the most deliberate public voice this person chose to project. Weight them accordingly — they reveal what this person considers worth broadcasting, not how they speak in dialogue.

Extract a behavioral profile precise enough to simulate how this person speaks and reacts in novel conversations.

Rules before you start:
- For relationship_matrix: only include accounts or figures this person explicitly addresses or mentions in these tweets. Do not invent relationships.

TRANSCRIPT-ONLY FIELDS — verbatim or nothing, no model knowledge:
- annotated_quotes: MINIMUM 10 quotes. Every quote must be copied verbatim from the tweets below. If fewer real quotes exist, produce fewer — never fabricate. Prioritize iconic, unmistakable lines each proving a DIFFERENT profile dimension.

MODEL KNOWLEDGE ALLOWED — supplement tweets where thin:
If you recognize {{ name }} from your training data, use that knowledge to enrich worldview, emotional_tells, response_patterns, and core_style with documented public behavior. For lesser-known figures, derive from tweets only.
NOTE: favored_words, structural_patterns, do_not_say are extracted separately without the tweets — do NOT include them in this response.

SPECIFICITY TEST — apply to every field before writing it:
Ask: "Could this exact description fit a different public figure without changing a word?" If yes, rewrite until the answer is no. Generic fillers like "engages with their audience", "values authenticity", "uses humor to connect" describe thousands of people. Every field must be falsifiable.

